<section class="wrap" style="max-width:70ch;">
  <h2 style="color:var(--teal-dark);">What children take away</h2>
  <p>Each book is set in a real Pacific location, featuring an animal that genuinely lives there. Children finish a Koa story knowing where Byron Bay is, what a goanna eats, why sea turtles come ashore, how a volcano forms — without ever feeling like they sat through a lesson. Curiosity comes before information. Discovery comes before explanation.</p>

  <h2 style="color:var(--teal-dark);margin-top:36px;">Our approach to the environment</h2>
  <p>Environmental care in Koa's world is always shown through positive action — helping a friend, cleaning a beach, protecting wildlife, working together. You will never find doom, guilt, or fear in these pages. The world is presented as something wonderful worth discovering and looking after, and children leave every story feeling capable, not anxious.</p>

  <h2 style="color:var(--teal-dark);margin-top:36px;">Our approach to culture</h2>
  <p>Each destination's people and traditions are treated with warmth and respect. Local friends are the experts of their own home — they teach Koa, never the other way around. Cultural elements are referenced with care, never used as decoration.</p>

  <h2 style="color:var(--teal-dark);margin-top:36px;">In the classroom and at home</h2>
  <p>The books pair naturally with geography (find each destination on a map), science (every animal is real and researchable), and values conversations (kindness, curiosity, teamwork). The free <a href="/activities/">Activities</a> section adds colouring pages and printables for every friend in the crew — and each new book brings a new place to explore together.</p>

